3. `c0efcac95f` — `attach_and_extract` (`src/Service/Extraction/`):
   upload → VLM-extract via Claude's native `document`/`image` content
   blocks → self-validate against `SchemaValidator` → store in OpenEMR →
   persist, all linked. New table `clinical_copilot_extracted_document`.
4. `5a09622bc4` — redesigned the Co-Pilot from an inline dashboard card
   into a slide-out sidebar (open by default, closeable, reopen tab),
   and fully wired the attach-document UI to (3) via a new
   `CopilotDocumentUploadController`.
5. `8e54e784aa` — added `get_extracted_documents` as a 5th chart-reading
   tool so the chat model can reference previously-uploaded documents in
   *later* turns, not just the upload's one-time confirmation message.
6. `2ec0bd293a` — 10 synthetic intake-form PDFs in `intake-forms/` for
   manually exercising the upload flow (`existing-patient/` ones are
   grounded in real dev-DB Synthea patients pid 2/7/18/20/25).
7. `a2e4042ff6` — fixed a partial-failure gap in (3): a document-storage
   failure now rolls back the already-inserted extraction row instead of
   leaving an orphan.
8. `8d0607fc75` — AgentForge2 Core Requirement #4, first pass:
   `Supervisor` + `ChartQaWorker` + `IntakeExtractorWorker`
   (`src/Service/Supervisor/`). **Not wired into `CopilotChatController`
   yet** — `CopilotService` (the original single-agent tool loop) is
   still the live entry point. Read `Supervisor.php`'s own class
   docblock before touching anything in this namespace — it documents a
   safety-relevant citation-granularity decision (claims must cite the
   specific tool, e.g. `get_medications`, never the worker name) that a
   PUNCH_LIST.md 1.4(b) guard depends on.

## What's explicitly NOT done (by design, not oversight)

- **Evidence-retriever worker + RAG subsystem**: not started at all. No
  corpus, no embeddings, no vector search, no reranker exist anywhere in
  this codebase. This needs its own scoping conversation before any
  code — it pulls in new infrastructure and cost decisions nothing else
  here has needed.
- **Supervisor is not the live entry point.** Swapping
  `CopilotChatController` from `CopilotService` to `Supervisor` is a
  real, un-taken next step.
- Stale git worktrees exist from earlier work
  (`docs/stage5-architecture-plan` missing, `agent-requirements`
  invalid, `video-script` partial — check `openemr-cmd worktree list`).
  Pre-existing, not created this session, not urgent.

## Environment/workflow gotchas worth knowing up front

- **Test iteration**: `openemr-cmd st`/`ut`/`pit` silently ignore
  `--filter` (documented in `Eval/README.md`). Use
  `docker exec development-easy-openemr-1 vendor/bin/phpunit [-c phpunit-isolated.xml] --filter <Class> --testdox`
  directly instead.
- **Always run PHPStan with `--memory-limit=1G`**, scoped to
  changed files only (`vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --memory-limit=1G <paths>`)
  — a full-codebase run is flaky/slow in this environment and CLAUDE.md's
  advice to always run full-codebase doesn't hold up in practice here.
- A custom PHPStan rule forbids catching bare `\Throwable` unless you
  immediately rethrow — narrow to the specific exception type instead
  (see `SqlExtractedDocumentStore`/`DocumentIngestionPipeline` for the
  pattern).
- `symfony/mime` is **not installed** in this project —
  `UploadedFile::getMimeType()` throws. Use PHP's native
  `mime_content_type()` on the real file path instead (see
  `CopilotDocumentUploadController`).
- This session did all testing against the **primary stack**
  (`development-easy` containers), not a worktree's own stack — a
  worktree's docker stack hit real disk pressure earlier in the session.
  Isolated/DB-backed tests don't need worktree isolation; only use
  `openemr-cmd worktree` machinery when you actually need a second,
  concurrently-running app instance.
- The Chrome extension (`claude-in-chrome`) was not connected in this
  environment. Browser verification was done via a Selenium/Panther
  script dropped into the bind-mounted `tmp/` dir, per CLAUDE.md's
  "Browser debugging via Selenium" section — use that pattern if
  `claude-in-chrome` still isn't available.
- Two pre-existing test failures are present in every full-suite run
  and are unrelated to any of this session's work:
  `CdaValidateDocumentsTest::testValidateDocumentWithCcdaTypeWithInvalidDocument`
  and `FieldRenderingSnapshotTest` (`edit visit-categories` data set).
  Don't chase these; confirm they're still the *only* two before
  concluding something new is a regression.

## Suggested skills for the next session

- Continue using `EnterPlanMode` + `AskUserQuestion` for any
  architecturally forked decision before writing code — every large
  piece this session (extraction pipeline, sidebar redesign, tool-loop
  wiring, Supervisor) went through that flow, and it's caught real
  design mistakes before they were built (e.g. the citation-granularity
  issue in Supervisor).
- `run` skill for driving the live app when `claude-in-chrome` isn't
  connected.
- The `eval-*-validator` skills (`.claude/skills/`) whenever touching
  the eval-gate layer.
- `grill-me` for any design with multiple real forks that benefits from
  being interviewed out loud before planning (used once this session for
  the factually-consistent validator's design).

## Natural next steps, roughly in order

1. Decide evidence-retriever/RAG scope (needs its own planning pass —
   don't start writing code without it).
2. Wire `Supervisor` into `CopilotChatController` as the live entry
   point, replacing `CopilotService` (with the same exhaustive
   CSRF/ACL/multi-patient-isolation test coverage
   `CopilotChatControllerTest` already has for the current path).
3. Once evidence-retriever exists, revisit the Supervisor's system
   prompt/tool list to add a third `consult_evidence_worker`.
